Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s assume ",
 StyleBox["\[Mu]11 > \[Mu]21 and \[Mu]22 > \[Mu]32",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " . Make sure that\[CloseCurlyQuote]s the case.\nLet pi be the prior \
probability of stimulus being in part i.\n\[Mu]ij is the mean of observation \
j when stimulus is in part i.\nLet rij be reward of choosing i when stimulus \
was in j.\nLet oi be the observation at time point i.\nLet \[Sigma] be the \
s.t.d of all distributions.\nIf o1 > \[Eta]1 we say stimulus in 1.\nIf o2 > \
\[Eta]2 we say stimulus in 2."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9088137100110197`*^9, 3.908813935842352*^9}, {
   3.908814078144105*^9, 3.908814103618381*^9}, {3.9088141922605352`*^9, 
   3.90881423131418*^9}, {3.9088143167359*^9, 3.908814409534336*^9}, {
   3.9088150913240967`*^9, 3.908815096569417*^9}, {3.908816393028627*^9, 
   3.908816402796625*^9}, {3.908816466642523*^9, 3.908816471567498*^9}, {
   3.909161324161105*^9, 3.90916132610991*^9}, 
   3.910178767134948*^9},ExpressionUUID->"417f15ad-a794-45a1-9e02-\
49912f0612e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s assume o1 and o2 are conditionally independent on \
s1.\nWe assume p(o1|s2) = p(o1|s3), i.e. ",
 StyleBox["\[Mu]21 = \[Mu]31\n",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Let \[Mu]21 = 0, and \[Mu]32 = 0. Since \[Mu]21 = 0, \[Mu]31 has to be 0 as \
well (by construction). \nLet all \[Sigma] be 1, W.L.O.G.\nNow I just have to \
ensure \[Mu]11 is positive and \[Mu]22 is positive."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9088137100110197`*^9, 3.908813935842352*^9}, {
  3.908814078144105*^9, 3.908814103618381*^9}, {3.9088141922605352`*^9, 
  3.90881423131418*^9}, {3.9088143167359*^9, 3.908814409534336*^9}, {
  3.9088147604469843`*^9, 3.908814781889391*^9}, {3.9088149670302258`*^9, 
  3.908814979045541*^9}, {3.908815931984974*^9, 3.908815946500112*^9}, {
  3.908820075560663*^9, 3.90882010370888*^9}, {3.910179358514523*^9, 
  3.910179358793181*^9}, {3.910179564466598*^9, 
  3.910179578155445*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ffc8b044-c3b1-4dc0-a724-\
768288df7374"],

