Cell["\<\
Choosing 3 is like missing.
Choosing 1 when it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s 2 or 3, and 2 when \
it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s 1 or 3, have their corresponding costs f1  and f2 \
respectively. 
Choosing 1 when it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s 1 and,  2 when it\[CloseCurlyQuote]s 2, \
reaps the food reward h.
f1, f2 < 0, and  h > 0.
Assuming all to have equal prior.
p1 = p2 = p3 = 1/3.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9088137100110197`*^9, 3.908813935842352*^9}, {
